  "summary": "Experience a comforting coastal classic with this <b>Italian slow braised squid</b> recipe featuring creamy white beans cooked in a rich garlic tomato broth. Slow braising transforms tender <b>squid rings</b> into melt-in-your-mouth morsels while allowing the savory seafood flavors to infuse the aromatic simmer sauce deeply. Nutritious <b>cannellini beans</b> absorb the aromatic blend of dry white wine, garlic, red pepper flakes, and tomatoes, adding a velvety texture and hearty substance to the dish. Finished with a touch of fresh flat leaf parsley and fine olive oil, this rustic seafood braise delivers authentic Mediterranean warmth in every spoonful. Serve this traditional meal hot with thick slices of crusty Italian bread to mop up every drop of the savory tomato broth. It is an ideal dish for relaxed weekend dinners when you want deep flavor with minimal active effort, showcasing how simple coastal ingredients come together into a satisfying and elegant homemade meal.",
